From 7b1b4971f0792eb81ef131540c6bf4a8c68b1aa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Kannegaard Hayes <philiphayes9@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:39:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] node: run --startup-notify once /readyz is ready and
 listeners are up

The hook ran at tip entry, before /readyz could answer ok, and before
Electrum and Esplora bound when the scripthash index lagged the tip
(they bind later, from the tip loop). A hook that starts services
depending on the node raced both.

Run it once, from the tip loop, after /readyz would first answer ok and
every configured Electrum and Esplora listener is bound. The readiness
check reads the store, so it runs on the blocking pool, and only until
the hook has run. A run that never enters tip follow (incomplete
catch-up, --max-run-secs 0) no longer runs the hook.
